.\" Revised Draft prepared from current source; see EDITORS-NOTES.md.
.\" Source: src/fft-gen.c
.TH "FFT-GEN" "1" "October 23, 2026" "ka9q-radio" "ka9q-radio Manual"
.SH NAME
fft-gen \- generate FFTW single-precision planning wisdom
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fft-gen
.RI "[options] [transform ...]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
fft-gen plans requested transforms and saves FFTW wisdom for subsequent use by
radiod. Transform specifications are read from arguments or, with no
arguments, one per line from standard input. Planning can be CPU intensive;
use the same machine and FFTW build as the receiver and preferably plan while
the machine is otherwise idle.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B "\-p, \-\-patient"
Use FFTW_PATIENT planning. This is the default.
.TP
.B "\-m, \-\-measure"
Use FFTW_MEASURE planning.
.TP
.B "\-x, \-\-exhaustive"
Use FFTW_EXHAUSTIVE planning.
.TP
.B "\-e, \-\-estimate"
Use FFTW_ESTIMATE planning.
.TP
.B "\-t seconds, \-\-timelimit seconds"
Set FFTW planning time limit for each requested transform. Default zero leaves
it unlimited.
.TP
.B "\-T threads, \-\-threads threads"
Set FFTW internal thread count. Default one. A nonpositive value skips
threaded FFTW initialization.
.TP
.B "\-f, \-\-force"
Do not import existing wisdom before planning; forget in-memory wisdom between
requested transforms. Saved wisdom is still merged with existing file
contents.
.TP
.B "\-v, \-\-verbose"
Increase diagnostics; repeat for detailed file and planner output.
.TP
.B "\-h, \-\-help"
Print usage and exit.
.SH TRANSFORM SPECIFICATIONS
Each specification consists of three letters followed by a positive transform
length. The first letter is c for complex or r for real. The second is i for
in-place, o for out-of-place with preserved input, or d for out-of-place with
input destruction permitted. The third is f for forward or b for backward.
.PP
Examples: rof750000 is a 750000-point out-of-place real forward transform;
cob1200 is a 1200-point out-of-place complex backward transform. Use the
transform sizes and thread count actually needed by the receiver.
.SH FILES
Existing wisdom is imported from FFTW's system wisdom, the application wisdom
file /var/lib/ka9q-radio/wisdom, and the version-specific file. Output is
saved to /var/lib/ka9q-radio/wisdom-VERSION-threaded when threaded planning is
enabled, or wisdom-VERSION otherwise. The state-directory path is configurable
at build time. File and directory permissions must permit updates; temporary
and lock files are used during saving.
.SH EXAMPLES
Generate plans or read requests from a file:
.PP
.nf
fft\-gen \-v \-T 1 rof750000 cob1200
fft\-gen \-v \-T 2 < /var/lib/ka9q\-radio/fft.log
.fi
.SH NOTES
The program can return
zero after reporting planning or file errors; check diagnostics and the
resulting wisdom file.
.SH SEE ALSO
radiod(8), fftwf-wisdom(1)
.PP
Project documentation: https://github.com/ka9q/ka9q-radio
